<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5973" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cădīvus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		cado (an access. form of caducus). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Of fruit, <i>falling of itself</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mala,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 16, 18, § 59</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">15, 17, 18,
				§ 60</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In medic. lang., <i>having the
				falling sickness</i> or <i>epilepsy</i>, <i>epileptic</i>, <i><span class="en">Marc. Emp.
			20</span></i>.</div>
